  "source": "Recorded from the Claude Code binary 2.1.289 (native linux-x64 build, `claude --version`) on a Linux machine, 2026-10-04: `claude -p 'run echo hi' --permission-mode default --allowedTools 'Bash(echo hi)' --output-format json` with ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL pointing at a local recorder that answered the first call with a Bash tool_use and the second with text, ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN a placeholder, ANTHROPIC_MODEL=engine-model, CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC=1, an empty CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR.",
  "redaction": "Claude Code is not open source: every string longer than 80 characters (its system prompt, tool descriptions, system reminders) and every schema `description` is replaced by a placeholder; paths, the device id and the session id are replaced. Keys, block types, roles, cache_control placement, tool names, schema structure, header names and every header value except the token are as sent.",
  "also_recorded": "beta_sets.auto_mode and auto_mode_body_keys: the same binary without --permission-mode (its -p default here is auto mode) adds the dangerous-tool-use and afk-mode betas and a top-level `safeguards` list (a classifier context with the user's paths and permission rules) to its first request. beta_sets.no_experimental: with CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_BETAS=1. Before its first call it sends an unauthenticated `HEAD /api/hello`.",
  "also_recorded_e9": "beta_sets.stream_json (E9, 2026-10-04): the same binary as the E9 adapter runs it, `claude -p --input-format stream-json --output-format stream-json --verbose --permission-mode dontAsk`, adds thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18 (with `thinking: {type: adaptive, display: updates}`) to every request."
